Observed by the k18 worker (2026-11-19): a local binary build at 7044aef extracted about 1650 entries, the deepest relative path 82 characters, including Moose exception classes, Specio and Perl::Tidy. The 0.001 CI probe had a deepest path of 45 characters, so this may be specific to the local build environment (scripts/loaded-modules.pl, scripts/binary-pp-args.sh). Matters for binary size, start-up cost and the PAR_TREE_RESERVE on Windows (128 since k18). Done when it is clear which run pulls these modules in, and the pp arguments pack only what the CLI loads, or a written note that the local build differs from CI on purpose.
